cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Assay
message: >-
  If you use Assay or implement the PromptFile format, please cite this
  repository. The specification is separately licensed CC BY 4.0 and may be
  implemented by anyone, including in competing products.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Baijayanta
    family-names: Roy
    alias: BaijayantaRoy
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
repository-code: https://github.com/BaijayantaRoy/Assay
url: https://baijayantaroy.github.io/Assay/
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An open, git-native engine for writing, running and proving out LLM prompts
  and agents. Prompts, agent harnesses and verified loops are stored as
  PromptFiles - readable text files carrying the template, model binding,
  guardrails and their own eval cases - and are exercised through a CLI, a REST
  API, an MCP server, SDKs and a web workbench. Its design commitment is that a
  reported number never overstates what was measured: an unverified loop reports
  not checked rather than passing, and a rate with no usable denominator is
  withheld rather than shown as zero.
keywords:
  - llm
  - prompt-engineering
  - agents
  - evaluation
  - ai-assurance
  - promptfile
  - mcp
